  "description": "A light palate-opening appetizer or the perfect accompaniment to a stir-fry or braise.",
  "notes": "Notes: This salad can be made with any variety of mature (i.e., not baby) spinach. Amaranth and hearty leafy greens, including kale, chard, and jìcài (shepherd’s purse), would all also be good.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The vinaigrette can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 1 week. The dressed salad can be refrigerated, covered, for up to 3 days, but will gradually lose its vibrant color.",
